    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d50">

                <pb facs="0163" n="71" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp01v01/pg71"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72119/8170</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Switzerland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Wilson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berne</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-02-03T18:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 3, 1918, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >February 4?</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">3 a.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2567. I am preparing important and long telegram supplementing my 2544, January
                    31, 4 p.m.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d50-f1"/> I venture to suggest that President
                    withhold any contemplated answer to Czernin until its recepit.<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d50-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Wilson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d50-f1" n="2" xml:id="d50-f1-content">
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Ante</hi>, <ref target="#pg60">p. 60</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d50-f2" n="3" xml:id="d50-f2-content">
                <p>The ensuing telegrams summarizing Professor Herron’s account of his conversations
                    with Lammasch are not printed; instead, the complete report rendered by pouch is
                    inserted <hi rendition="#italic">post</hi>, <ref target="#pg82">p. 82</ref>, in
                    the order of date of receipt of the last of the series of telegrams, Feb. 7,
                    9.43 a.m.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
